# Exception: a real (not synthetic) pipeline-generated database, committed
# deliberately so the Zeelandbrug opening-bridge regression test exercises
# genuine navmesh/skeleton geometry — the bugs it guards against (SSFA
# portal-vertex swap, A* goal-test ignoring funnel suffix cost, mariculture
# obstacle over-blocking) only ever surfaced on a real generated database,
# never on the small synthetic fixtures used by the other navmesh tests.
!test/fixtures/zeelandbrug/netherlands.sqlite
**/repomix-output.xml
**/*.pyc
backend/__pycache__/nautical_routing_pipeline.cpython-312.pyc

# Data-repo staging files (sync to signalk-router-data repo)
router-data/
backend/deploy_to_data_repo.py
signalk-routeiq-*.tgz

